# Push changes after every task

When you finish implementing or fixing something in this repo:

1. Run `git status` — if there are no changes, do not create an empty commit.
2. Stage only relevant files (never `.env`, `.env.local`, or secrets).
3. Commit with a clear message describing why the change was made.
4. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`) unless the user asked not to push.

Do this at the end of the task without waiting for the user to ask, unless they explicitly said not to commit or push in that conversation.
